    // ============================================================================
    // The Forsaken Realms - Restricted Cards list. Any card named here is
    // excluded from the main reward/shop/booster pool AND sourceDeck-based
    // rewards (e.g. the Alt-Art boss-reward decks), no matter how many printings
    // of it a reward deck happens to list. Add card names below (exact spelling)
    // as more problem cards turn up - no code change needed, just restart the
    // game. Comments (// lines) are supported by the game's JSON reader - leave
    // them in.
    //
    // NOT covered by this list (2026-08-22 review finding, still open): colored
    // booster shops (AdventureEventController.generateBoosterByColor() - full
    // card DB minus edition filtering only), a cardPackShop reward that sets an
    // explicit editions list, fixed "cardPack" deck rewards, and an explicit
    // cardName/cardUnion cardName reward. A card added here can still reach the
    // player through one of those paths - see RewardData.java.
    //
    // Moved here 2026-08-22 (was inline in config.json) so the list has its own
    // easy-to-edit home, same as settings.json - see MOD_CHANGELOG.md.
    //
    // Round 387 (a player on Discord: "there shouldn't be commander specific cards in the
    // pool and in enemy decks (like arcane signet and command tower)"): commanderOnlyCards
    // below lists every card that does nothing - or breaks - without a commander. They are
    // restricted like everything here, AND taken out of every ENEMY deck as it loads
    // (swapped for a basic land of the deck's main color - the restricted list itself never
    // touched enemy decks, so 600+ decks still played Arcane Signet). Boosters now honor
    // BOTH lists too (a restricted card in a pack is swapped for another card of the same
    // rarity from the same set). Grep forge.log for [TFR-CommanderCards].
